014b82e0-02db-4737-93e0-07d8c416e271	68794c8a-1d53-4905-bb6b-5e3af852501d	1	Document Name: Testing\nCategory: Test\nSub-Category: Test 1\nLine Number: 60 to 100\nVersion: v1\nUpdated Date: -\n\n---\n\n- Access control and permissions - Positive and negative scenarios - Boundary and exception scenarios AI-Assisted Test Case Generation QA team may use AI tools to generate initial test cases. However: - All AI-generated test cases must be reviewed by QA. - Test cases should be aligned with business requirements. - QA is responsible for the final accuracy and completeness of test coverage. Test Execution Testing activities may include: - Functional Testing - Validation Testing - Integration Testing - User Acceptance Support - Regression Testing - Retesting Defect Management - All defects shall be logged in Meld-EP. - Defects should contain proper reproduction steps, screenshots, and severity. - Defect status shall be tracked until closure. Retesting and Regression Testing Retesting - Retesting is performed after defect fixes are received. - A note must be maintained indicating the retested defects and their outcomes. Regression Testing - Regression testing must be linked to the respective release. - Regression test execution and results should be documented release-wise. - Regression reports must be stored in the designated OneDrive folder. Test Closure QA shall prepare: - Test Execution Report - Defect Summary Report - Regression Testing Summary - QA Sign-off	[0.41502017,0.21554095,-3.2876964,-0.92060417,1.4012221,-0.39722756,1.5221705,0.15207978,0.24191739,-0.32623205,0.77619857,0.75246984,0.9105045,0.39762372,-0.91588557,-1.026018,0.4513536,-0.74710536,-0.5822512,-0.49104887,0.35499236,-0.56457454,-1.715724,-0.42944157,1.2521981,0.3607618,-1.0219238,0.45204476,-1.1543114,-0.7476299,0.04656808,-0.34701917,0.804138,-0.730449,-0.6990749,-0.80544907,1.1582729,0.533008,-0.21815827,0.7539803,0.93333584,-0.4702272,0.19684814,-0.36972612,0.2466271,0.33455548,1.3624219,0.5484