COPY public.new_sop_documents (id, meldep_id, title, category, sub_category, version, status, document_is_active, purpose, content, created_by, created_date, updated_by, updated_date, metadata_created_at_utc, metadata_updated_at_utc, metadata_is_active, upload_status) FROM stdin;
ed09c9ea-9850-4dac-8186-7edc584191d1	1234	testing_process	Engineer	SDLC	1.0	Published	t	The purpose of STLC is to ensure that software is tested systematically, defects are identified and resolved, and the delivered product meets business and user requirements.	Title: Testing Process\nCategory: Engineer\nSub Category: SDLC\nVersion: 1.0\nStatus: Published\nIs Active: Active\nCreated By: Bhagyashri Pednekar\nCreated Date: 06/16/2026\nUpdated By: Bhagyashri Pednekar\nUpdated Date: 07/03/2026\n\nPurpose\nThe purpose of STLC is to ensure that software is tested systematically, defects are identified and resolved, and the delivered product meets business and user requirements.\n\nEntry Criteria\nBefore testing begins, ensure:\n- Requirement is documented and available in Meld-EP / Task.\n- Requirement understanding is completed.\n- Necessary access is provided.\n- Test environment is available.\n\nTest Planning\n\nTest Plan Preparation\nQA team shall prepare a Test Plan containing:\n- Scope of testing\n- Testing approach\n- Resources involved\n- Timeline\n- OneDrive folder path for all testing-related documents\n\nDocument Repository\nAll testing-related documents must be maintained in a centralized OneDrive folder, including:\n- Test Plan\n- Test Cases\n- Test Execution Reports\n- Defect Reports\n- Release-wise Regression Testing Reports\nThe OneDrive folder path should be mentioned in the Test Plan document.\n\nTest Case Design\nBefore writing test cases, QA should understand:\n- Business process driving the requirement\n- End user and user roles\n- Use cases and workflows\n- Access permissions\n- UI look and feel requirements\n- Functional requirements\n- Validations\n- Data requirements\n\nTest Coverage\nTest cases should cover:\n- CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete)\n- Dropdowns and selection controls\n- Mandatory field validations\n- Business rule validations\n- UI verification\n- Data verification\n- Access control and permissions\n- Positive and negative scenarios\n- Boundary and exception scenarios\n\nAI-Assisted Test Case Generation\nQA team may use AI tools to generate initial test cases. However:\n- All AI-generated test cases must be reviewed by QA.\n- Test cases should be aligned with business requirements.\n- QA is responsible for the final accuracy and completeness of test coverage.\n\nTest Execution\nTesting activities may include:\n- Functional Testing\n- Validation Testing\n- Integration Testing\n- User Acceptance Support\n- Regression Testing\n- Retesting\n\nDefect Management\n- All defects shall be logged in Meld-EP.\n- Defects should contain proper reproduction steps, screenshots, and severity.\n- Defect status shall be tracked until closure.\n\nRetesting and Regression Testing\n\nRetesting\n- Retesting is performed after defect fixes are received.\n- A note must be maintained indicating the retested defects and their outcomes.\n\nRegression Testing\n- Regression testing must be linked to the respective release.\n- Regression test execution and results should be documented release-wise.\n- Regression reports must be stored in the designated OneDrive folder.\n\nTest Closure\nQA shall prepare:\n- Test Execution Report\n- Defect Summary Report\n- Regression Testing Summary\n- QA Sign-off\n	Bhagyashri Pednekar	\N	Bhagyashri Pednekar	\N	2026-07-22 12:04:35.813171+05:30	2026-07-23 20:22:53.716498+05:30	f	Uploaded
d7fe9c57-e0ef-4202-a263-9abf41a5d456	4321	SDLC Module	Engineer	SDLC	1.0	Published	t	Deliver software efficiently and consistently. Maintain quality and security standards. Improve communication among teams. Ensure project visibility and traceability. Reduce project risks and production defects. Support future audits and compliance activities	Title: SDLC Module\nCategory: Engineer\nSub Category: SDLC\nVersion: 1.0\nStatus: Published\nIs Active: Active\n\nWhat is SDLC in our organization?\nSDLC (Software Development Life Cycle) defines how a project moves from Requirement to Development to Testing to Deployment to Maintenance to Security and Governance.\nIt ensures:\n- Structured development\n- Quality assurance\n- Controlled deployment\n- Traceability of work\n- Compliance readiness\n\nWhich tools are used across SDLC phases?\nSDLC Phase: Requirement Analysis -- Tools Used: Meld-EP, OneDrive, Email\nSDLC Phase: Development -- Tools Used: VS Code, Visual Studio, GitHub, TFS, OneDrive\nSDLC Phase: Testing (QA) -- Tools Used: Meld-EP, Excel\nSDLC Phase: Deployment -- Tools Used: GitHub, VS Code, SQL\nSDLC Phase: Maintenance and Support -- Tools Used: Meld-EP, GCP, Teams, OneDrive\nSDLC Phase: Architecture and Design -- Tools Used: Figma, Canva, Gamma, OneDrive\nSDLC Phase: Information Security -- Tools Used: Meld-EP, Teams, OneDrive\n\nHow are the requirements collected?\nRequirements are gathered through:\n- Meld-EP Project Folder\n- Client discussions\n- Emails\n- Team meetings\n\nWhere are the requirements documented?\nRequirements are stored in:\n- Project Folder\n- OneDrive documentation repository\n\nHow is feasibility decided?\nThrough:\n- Technical discussion\n- Stakeholder meetings\n- Email approvals\n\nHow are priorities defined?\nRequirements are prioritized during team meetings based on:\n- Business impact\n- Urgency\n- Development effort\n\nHow are requirement changes handled?\nChange Requests are managed via:\n- Email communication\n- Team meetings\n- Updated documentation\n\nHow is requirement traceability maintained?\nTraceability is maintained using:\n- Meld-EP tracking\n- Meeting discussions\n- Documentation updates\n\nWho prepares the Test Plan?\nQA team prepares the Test Strategy and Test Plan in Meld-EP.\n\nWhere are test cases created?\nTest cases are created and managed in:\n- Meld-EP\n\nHow is test execution performed?\nManual testing is done using:\n- Meld-EP\n- Excel (when required)\n\nHow are defects tracked?\nAll defects are logged in:\n- Meld-EP Issue Tracking\n\nWhat testing types are performed?\n- Functional Testing\n- Regression Testing\n- Manual Testing\n- Validation Testing\n\nHow is testing closed?\nQA generates:\n- Test Report\n- QA Sign-off\n\nHow are incidents reported?\nThrough:\n- Email\n- Team meetings\n- Meld-EP tracking\n\nHow is root cause analysis done?\nRCA is conducted during team discussions after issue investigation.\n\nHow are bugs fixed post-release?\nFixes are implemented via:\n- VS Code / Visual Studio\n- GitHub patch release\n	Bhagyashri Pednekar	\N	Bhagyashri Pednekar	\N	2026-07-22 16:58:48.444554+05:30	2026-07-23 20:22:55.621202+05:30	f	Completed
68794c8a-1d53-4905-bb6b-5e3af852501d	4321	Testing	Test	Test 1	v1	Published	t	\N	Title: Testing Process\nCategory: Engineer\nSub Category: SDLC\nVersion: 1.0\nStatus: Published\nIs Active: Active\nCreated By: Bhagyashri Pednekar\nCreated Date: 06/16/2026\nUpdated By: Bhagyashri Pednekar\nUpdated Date: 07/03/2026\n\nPurpose\nThe purpose of STLC is to ensure that software is tested systematically, defects are identified and resolved, and the delivered product meets business and user requirements.\n\nEntry Criteria\nBefore testing begins, ensure:\n- Requirement is documented and available in Meld-EP / Task.\n- Requirement understanding is completed.\n- Necessary access is provided.\n- Test environment is available.\n\nTest Planning\n\nTest Plan Preparation\nQA team shall prepare a Test Plan containing:\n- Scope of testing\n- Testing approach\n- Resources involved\n- Timeline\n- OneDrive folder path for all testing-related documents\n\nDocument Repository\nAll testing-related documents must be maintained in a centralized OneDrive folder, including:\n- Test Plan\n- Test Cases\n- Test Execution Reports\n- Defect Reports\n- Release-wise Regression Testing Reports\nThe OneDrive folder path should be mentioned in the Test Plan document.\n\nTest Case Design\nBefore writing test cases, QA should understand:\n- Business process driving the requirement\n- End user and user roles\n- Use cases and workflows\n- Access permissions\n- UI look and feel requirements\n- Functional requirements\n- Validations\n- Data requirements\n\nTest Coverage\nTest cases should cover:\n- CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete)\n- Dropdowns and selection controls\n- Mandatory field validations\n- Business rule validations\n- UI verification\n- Data verification\n- Access control and permissions\n- Positive and negative scenarios\n- Boundary and exception scenarios\n\nAI-Assisted Test Case Generation\nQA team may use AI tools to generate initial test cases. However:\n- All AI-generated test cases must be reviewed by QA.\n- Test cases should be aligned with business requirements.\n- QA is responsible for the final accuracy and completeness of test coverage.\n\nTest Execution\nTesting activities may include:\n- Functional Testing\n- Validation Testing\n- Integration Testing\n- User Acceptance Support\n- Regression Testing\n- Retesting\n\nDefect Management\n- All defects shall be logged in Meld-EP.\n- Defects should contain proper reproduction steps, screenshots, and severity.\n- Defect status shall be tracked until closure.\n\nRetesting and Regression Testing\n\nRetesting\n- Retesting is performed after defect fixes are received.\n- A note must be maintained indicating the retested defects and their outcomes.\n\nRegression Testing\n- Regression testing must be linked to the respective release.\n- Regression test execution and results should be documented release-wise.\n- Regression reports must be stored in the designated OneDrive folder.\n\nTest Closure\nQA shall prepare:\n- Test Execution Report\n- Defect Summary Report\n- Regression Testing Summary\n- QA Sign-off\n	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-23 20:24:08.490653+05:30	2026-07-23 20:24:08.803284+05:30	t	Completed
